WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
The sage Hillel asked
three famous questions.

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:07.010
If I am not for myself,
who will be for me?

3
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.090
If I am only for myself, what am I?

4
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.230
If not now, when?

5
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.720
His words are kept in the Mishnah,
in an order about damages,

6
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:17.640
courts and judges.

7
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:22.050
So why does a book of Jewish law contain
a chapter of advice on how to be a good

8
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.150
person?

9
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.560
In this mission, you'll follow
a chain of teachers from Sinai,

10
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.620
and the three things they said.

11
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.630
Then you'll find out what,
according to the sages,

12
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.020
the whole world stands on.

13
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: find out why advice on
being a good person sits inside a book of

14
00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:39.550
law.
